@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.786 = private unnamed_addr constant [641 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary dict comprehension when creating a dictionary from\0Aan iterable.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to use a dict comprehension to build a dictionary from\0Aan iterable when the value is static.\0A\0APrefer `dict.fromkeys(iterable)` over `{value: None for value in iterable}`,\0Aas `dict.fromkeys` is more readable and efficient.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A{a: None for a in iterable}\0A{a: 1 for a in iterable}\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adict.fromkeys(iterable)\0Adict.fromkeys(iterable, 1)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `dict.fromkeys`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#dict.fromkeys)\0A", align 1
