@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.1037 = private unnamed_addr constant [863 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for conditional blocks gated on `sys.version_info` comparisons\0Athat are outdated for the minimum supported Python version.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python, code can be conditionally executed based on the active\0APython version by comparing against the `sys.version_info` tuple.\0A\0AIf a code block is only executed for Python versions older than the\0Aminimum supported version, it should be removed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info < (3, 0):\0A    print(\22py2\22)\0Aelse:\0A    print(\22py3\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aprint(\22py3\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `target-version`\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe because it will remove all code,\0Acomments, and annotations within unreachable version blocks.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `sys.version_info`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#sys.version_info)\0A", align 1
