@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.1059 = private unnamed_addr constant [1291 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for non-raw literal string arguments passed to the `match` parameter\0Aof `pytest.raises()` where the string contains at least one unescaped\0Aregex metacharacter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `match` argument is implicitly converted to a regex under the hood.\0AIt should be made explicit whether the string is meant to be a regex or a \22plain\22 pattern\0Aby prefixing the string with the `r` suffix, escaping the metacharacter(s)\0Ain the string using backslashes, or wrapping the entire string in a call to\0A`re.escape()`.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Awith pytest.raises(Exception, match=\22A full sentence.\22):\0A    do_thing_that_raises()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Awith pytest.raises(Exception, match=r\22A full sentence.\22):\0A    do_thing_that_raises()\0A```\0A\0AAlternatively:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0Aimport re\0A\0A\0Awith pytest.raises(Exception, match=re.escape(\22A full sentence.\22)):\0A    do_thing_that_raises()\0A```\0A\0Aor:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0Aimport re\0A\0A\0Awith pytest.raises(Exception, \22A full sentence\\\\.\22):\0A    do_thing_that_raises()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `re.escape`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/re.html#re.escape)\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.raises`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-raises)\0A", align 1
